/E (Holmes here warns us that there is no promise that truth will emerge from the competition of the market - you can't be sure that the best or most correct ideas will catch on. )
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
651 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1346 0 R
/E (But what it means to live in the American democracy, he says, is that you have to believe in that process of experimentation and trial and error, and that public opinion - even if based on imperfect knowledge - should be the guide to determining what is correct.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
